WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.603
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with J.B. Smoove.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:04.737
Alright, we heard Pizza Table.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.138
Do you have
another "Shark Tank" for us?

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:07.406
-Of course I do.
This is amazing.

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:09.042
This is going to
revolutionize relationships.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:12.478
It's called What I Say?
It's called What I Say?

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:14.580
It's an app, right?
It's an app.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.881
So, when you're in an argument,

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:18.050
the main thing about
an argument is this.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.419
"You didn't say that.
You didn't say that."

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:22.055
"Yes, I did. Yes, I did."

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.423
So, it's called What I Say?

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:27.260
And it rewinds your life
or this moment, right?

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.230
It records the last minute or
two of the conversation.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.698
So you can always go back.

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:34.534
It works the same way as

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.068
your security cameras
in your home.

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:40.106
It just naturally stays on and
records the argument.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:43.610
And it has a unique sensor
that senses

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:48.047
an argument about to happen,
and it comes on automatically.

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:50.816
And you program your app
to a certain volume

00:00:50.816 --> 00:00:52.451
so that if she's yelling
from the room,

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:54.820
you got to set it
from where it's at.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.589
And then can you go back.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.157
"I didn't say that."
"Yes, you did."

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:00.259
And you hit the button
on the app,

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:02.529
and it will play back
what the hell you just said.

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:04.063
See? It's called What I Say?

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.598
What I Say?

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.833
What did I say?
What did I say?

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:10.136
How did this happen?
Why are we arguing right now?

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.672
What happened?
What did I say?!

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.474
-It's really good, J.B.
-Isn't that great?

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:17.476
-I want to congratulate you
on the fact

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:20.513
that you're Emmy-nominated for
"Mapleworth Murders."

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:23.115
You're -- One of your
fellow nominees

00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:26.752
is the co-creator of the show,
our old friend John Lutz.

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:28.955
But there's also some --
You know, not that

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.490
you guys aren't heavy hitters,

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:34.660
but you're also in the category
with Kevin Hart, John Travolta.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:37.496
Pretty good list.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:41.167
It's a good list, Seth.
And here's what I'm saying.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:44.536
I think John and I -- One of us
has a great chance to win this.

00:01:44.536 --> 00:01:46.839
-When you say "John,"
do you mean Lutz or Travolta?

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:47.840
-John Lutz.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.308
John Lutz and I, I feel,

00:01:49.308 --> 00:01:53.178
have a great, great chance
to win this.

00:01:53.178 --> 00:01:55.548
You know, people love --
People love John Travolta.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:56.649
You know?

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.084
And I'm just worried
that they may --

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.618
You know how
they give people awards

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:01.553
for something
they previously did?

00:02:01.553 --> 00:02:02.755
I just don't want it to happen.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.591
I don't want them
to give him this Emmy

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:09.095
for this show he did based on
"Saturday Night Fever."

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.397
I don't want this to happen.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.999
I just don't want
this to happen.

00:02:13.999 --> 00:02:15.234
It happens all the time.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.002
-Yeah.
-You know, it happens.

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:19.873
They give you an award for
something you did previously,

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:21.174
and I don't want that to happen.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.308
I don't want that to happen.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:26.479
Or he gets that Sweathog
sympathy, you know,

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:27.680
from being a damn Sweathog.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.049
I don't want that either.
-No. I mean, come on.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.985
To the vo-- If any voters
are watching, please,

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:34.787
save us your Sweathog sympathy.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.022
Now, I will say --
-Don't do that.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.856
-J.B., J.B.,
would you be honest?

00:02:37.856 --> 00:02:39.592
Would you be honest --
Be honest with me.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:42.695
Would you be okay if people
gave you some Leon love?

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.597
Like, if they're like, "Oh, I
loved him as Leon on 'Curb,'

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.732
so I'm going to vote for him,"

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.800
do -- Will you accept that vote?

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.468
-I'll be disappointed.

00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:51.637
You know, I've been on that
damn show six seasons.

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:55.308
Five, six seasons now.
I don't need no sympathy award.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.476
I wouldn't --
You know what I would do?

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:58.645
I would give it to John.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.246
I would give it to John
if I won it.

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:02.515
It's John's.
Take it! Take it!

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:03.850
I don't want that sympathy.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.218
But here's what I recommend.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:07.653
If John should win, here's what
I think we should do.

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:08.954
We're a team on the same show.

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:10.123
Here's what I think
we should do.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:14.861
We should make this Emmy
like the Stanley Cup.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:19.031
See? We share it
and we both have it

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:21.934
for a certain amount of time
and we go on tour with it

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:25.004
and we raise it above our head
and go places with it.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:27.807
Because, you know, we won this.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.909
It's the same damn show.
We're on the same damn show.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:33.579
-Now, this show
was originally on Quibi,

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.514
and now you can
watch it on Roku.

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:39.285
Did you have Roku before
"Mapleworth" went to Roku?

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.752
-No, I did not have it.

00:03:40.752 --> 00:03:43.589
Now, all these weird names
throw me off a little bit.

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:47.694
Quibi sounds like a small,
little town in Canada somewhere.

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:49.261
Doesn't it? It has a ring to it.

00:03:49.261 --> 00:03:51.463
Like, "I'm going over to Quibi
for the weekend."

00:03:51.463 --> 00:03:52.832
You know what I mean?

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:56.702
And Roku sound like one of
those delicious sushi rolls

00:03:56.702 --> 00:03:59.004
at one of those places,
you know?

00:03:59.004 --> 00:04:00.740
Doesn't it sound like that?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.574
-Or a hot pepper.

00:04:02.574 --> 00:04:05.677
Like, it's 10 times as hot
as a jalapeño.

00:04:05.677 --> 00:04:08.547
Like, the Roku pepper
or something like that.

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:12.285
Doesn't it sound --
It reminds me of something

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.720
you're not supposed to eat,

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.520
but, somehow,
somebody made it cool.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:16.555
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:17.924
It's, like, undigestible,

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:20.292
so it goes in and comes out
the same way.

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:22.228
You know what I'm saying?
You can't even chew it.

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:25.331
You got to swallow it,
like a pill, you know?

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.266
That's the Roku pepper.

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:29.535
-Well, I definitely think,
when they named the app,

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:32.705
they were hoping people
would come to this conclusion.

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.006
-You know what?
I think they would.

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:35.508
-Yeah.
-I think they should.

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:39.712
-Anything that has
J.B. Smoove is

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:42.114
10 times hotter than a jalapeño.

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:43.316
Let me tell you that much.

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:44.717
-Whoo!

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:49.755
See? You know me so well,
because, normally --

00:04:49.755 --> 00:04:51.356
I'mma tell you something
about you.

00:04:51.356 --> 00:04:55.294
A lot of times, you know,
I feel like you debunk.

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:57.630
You are a debunker.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.766
-I'm a debunker?
-You're a debunker.

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:01.700
You know what a debunker is?

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.637
You debunk some things that
I say sometimes

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:07.840
like you don't believe
exactly what I'm saying.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.175
-J.B., I'm going to let you go,

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:11.977
because we all want you to
finish that drink.

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:14.079
-Oh, it's delicious.

00:05:14.079 --> 00:05:17.450
Hey, you should -- When you hold
a drink in your hand,

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.951
it makes people comfortable.

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.886
You should do
that on your show, Seth.

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:21.988
You should have
a little cocktail

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:23.690
in your hand and always do this.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.525
"Now, you people know
out there..."

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.426
You know, and then do
your whole monologue

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:29.329
with a drink in your hand,
you know?

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:31.196
Some people say a drink
in your hand

00:05:31.196 --> 00:05:34.400
and one hand down the front of
your pants like Al Bundy,

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.701
but I think that's too far.

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:38.303
I think that's too much.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.303 --> 00:05:39.538
-"Mapleworth Murders"

00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:41.240
is streaming now on
The Roku Channel.

